.SS PEB_GET_MODULE_BASE
.IP
.EX
void    *PEB_GET_MODULE_BASE(const char *);
void    *peb_get_module_base(const char *);
.EE
.PP
Searches the process loader\(aqs module list through the PEB and returns
the base address of a loaded module whose Unicode filename matches the
target argument.
.PP
The function traverses the loader\(aqs \f[CR]InLoadOrderModuleList\f[R],
compares each module\(aqs \f[CR]BaseDllName\f[R], and returns the
corresponding \f[CR]DllBase\f[R] when a match is found.
.PP
Returns:
.IP \(bu 2
Module base address on success.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]0\f[R] if the module is not loaded.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]0\f[R] if the PEB or loader structures are unavailable.
.PP
Example:
.IP
.EX
void    *KERNEL32 = PEB_GET_MODULE_BASE(\(dqKERNEL32.DLL\(dq);

\f[B]if\f[R] (!KERNEL32)
{
    \f[I]/* Module somehow not found */\f[R]
}
\f[B]else\f[R]
{
    \f[I]/* KERNEL32.DeleteFileA(\(dqKERNEL32.DLL\(dq) */\f[R]
}
.EE
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS PEB_GET_EXPORT
.IP
.EX
void    *PEB_GET_EXPORT(const unsigned char *, const char *);
void    *peb_get_export(const unsigned char *, const char *);
.EE
.PP
Retrieves the address of an exported function by manually parsing a
module\(aqs PE export directory.
.PP
The function validates the DOS header, locates the PE header, resolves
the export table, and performs a string comparison against exported
names until the requested symbol is found.
.PP
Unlike \f[CR]GetProcAddress()\f[R], no Windows API calls are used.
.PP
Returns:
.IP \(bu 2
Exported function address on success.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]0\f[R] if the export does not exist.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]0\f[R] if the module is invalid or lacks an export table.
.PP
Example:
.IP
.EX
#define INCL_CMT_STDCALL
#include \f[B]<CMT.H>\f[R] \f[I]// STDCALL\f[R]

void    *KERNEL32 = PEB_GET_MODULE_BASE(\(dqKERNEL32.DLL\(dq);

\f[B]typedef\f[R] void    *(STDCALL *FN_GETPROCADDRESS)(void *, const char *);

FN_GETPROCADDRESS   GET_PROC_ADDRESS = (FN_GETPROCADDRESS)PEB_GET_EXPORT(KERNEL32, \(dqGetProcAddress\(dq);

\f[B]if\f[R] (GET_PROC_ADDRESS)
{
    \f[I]/* Export resolved */\f[R]
    \f[I]/* You can now use GetProcAddress function as GET_PROC_ADDRESS */\f[R]
}
.EE
